# MindView _redirects — Cloudflare Pages URL routing
# Rules evaluated top-to-bottom; first match wins.
# Updated 2026-06-03.
#
# KEY PRINCIPLE: Cloudflare Pages AUTOMATICALLY serves every .html file
# at its clean URL with no rules needed:
#   catalog.html     → accessible at /catalog AND /catalog.html
#   enrolment.html   → accessible at /enrolment AND /enrolment.html
#   courses/mcr3u.html → accessible at /courses/mcr3u AND /courses/mcr3u.html
#
# Adding redirect/rewrite rules for these creates redirect loops because
# CF Pages strips .html internally before matching _redirects rules,
# then the rule sends it back to the .html URL → infinite loop.
#
# Only add rules here for paths that DON'T have a matching .html file
# on disk (auth routes, function routes, typo heals, security blocks).

# ── Auth: /login and /admin have matching .html files in subdirectories
#    so they need explicit rules (subdirectory files don't get auto-clean-URLs) ──
/login                  /admin/login.html               200
/admin                  /admin/dashboard.html           200

# ── Typo heal: /course/:code (singular, missing 's') → correct URL ───
# Only fires for paths like /course/eng4u — NOT /courses/eng4u.html
/course/:code           /courses/:code.html             301

# ── Security: block dev/config files from being served ───────────────
/app.py                 /404.html                       404
/users.db               /404.html                       404
/.secret_key            /404.html                       404
/wrangler.toml          /404.html                       404
/package.json           /404.html                       404
/.env                   /404.html                       404
/.env.local             /404.html                       404
